docker/demo.sh: mount the host's SIPL driver directories into the demo container, read-only.

SIPL loads camera drivers from /usr/lib/nvsipl_uddf (UDDF drivers, e.g. the D555's
libnvuddf_realsense_library.so) and /usr/lib/nvsipl_drv (e.g. the D457 module driver and query
plugin). The container has neither, so a SIPL player run inside it cannot find the camera driver.
Each mount is added only when the directory exists on the host.

diff --git a/docker/demo.sh b/docker/demo.sh
index 3903d61..173a4b3 100755
--- a/docker/demo.sh
+++ b/docker/demo.sh
@@ -98,6 +98,8 @@ docker run \
     -v /tmp/argus_socket:/tmp/argus_socket \
     -v /sys/devices:/sys/devices \
     -v /var/nvidia/nvcam/settings:/var/nvidia/nvcam/settings \
+    $(if [ -d /usr/lib/nvsipl_uddf ]; then echo "-v /usr/lib/nvsipl_uddf:/usr/lib/nvsipl_uddf:ro"; fi) \
+    $(if [ -d /usr/lib/nvsipl_drv ]; then echo "-v /usr/lib/nvsipl_drv:/usr/lib/nvsipl_drv:ro"; fi) \
     -w $PWD \
     -e NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES=graphics,video,compute,utility,display \
     -e NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=all \
